    <briefdescription>
<para>BoundedExecutor configured for the synchronous database path. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Runs blocking database work (permission checks, queries, response building) off the Drogon IO threads. Worker count and queue capacity come from configuration in the default constructor; the other constructor allows explicit sizes for tests. When configured, requests may first be attempted on the IO thread via a <ref refid="classDbProbe" kindref="compound">DbProbe</ref> (see <ref refid="classDbExecutor_1a5d6abf2368cd71250974124d570b7f2b" kindref="member">ioFastPath()</ref>). Thread-safety and shutdown semantics are inherited from BoundedExecutor. <simplesect kind="see"><para>BoundedExecutor, <ref refid="classDbProbe" kindref="compound">DbProbe</ref>, <ref refid="dbexecutor_8hpp_1a936968e57939fceaf59b5600a46630aa" kindref="member">runOnDbExecutor</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
